hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15503","Rawh narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, and Abdullah ibn al-Harith said: Ibn Jurayj presented to me, he said: Amr ibn Abi Sufyan informed me that Amr ibn Abi Safwan informed him, al-Dahhak and Abdullah ibn al-Harith said: That Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan informed him that Kaladah ibn al-Hanbal informed him that Safwan ibn Umayyah sent him at the Conquest with liba and judayah and daghabis, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at the upper part of the valley, he said: So I entered upon him without giving salam and without seeking permission, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go back and say: al-Salamu alaykum, may I enter, after Safwan had become Muslim. Amr said: Umayyah ibn Safwan informed me of this report, and he did not say: I heard it from Kaladah. Al-Dahhak and Ibn al-Harith said: And that was after he had become Muslim, and al-Dahhak and Abdullah ibn al-Harith said: With laban and judayah."
